(ned -- SET C REF, operator spec 2026-08-03. ONE PRESS, no recording.)
(It asserts the zero, steps 1 in in front, tilts A to -45 about the)
(calibrated A zero, and raises the puck -- then hands control back so the)
(operator can jog the tip to where driving toward centre in +X would strike)
(the puck.)

(THE OPERATOR THEN PRESSES StartC, AND THAT captures the jogged pose. There)
(is no second press of this button: one button, one job.)

(#3059 = 1 means "positioned, awaiting the jog". cal_c_zero clears it when it)
(takes the reading.)

o<cal_c_ref> sub
  #<cx>  = #1
  #<cy>  = #2
  #<top> = #3

  #<safe>  = 5.0        (operator 2026-08-03: 5 mm for every cal routine)
  #<front> = 25.4       (1 inch in FRONT of centre, X- side)

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, SET C REF: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, SET C REF: no puck centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif

  G90
  (1. START FROM THE ZERO, not from wherever the head was left)
  (   -- operator 2026-08-03. Rise only if low; never drive Z down to clear.)
  o20 if [#5422 LT [#<top> + #<safe>]]
    G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F2500
  o20 endif
  G1 A#3069 C#3070 F1200
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F2500
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<safe>] F2500

  (2. step off centre BEFORE tilting. A 45 deg roll moves the tip far)
  (   further than 5 mm, so tilting directly over the puck would drive into)
  (   it. In front keeps the puck out from under the swing.)
  G1 X[#<cx> - #<front>] F2500

  (3. tilt about the CALIBRATED A zero, not the stale DRO zero)
  G1 A[#3069 - 45] F1200

  (4. puck UP and settled BEFORE control returns, so the operator jogs)
  (   against the surface they will actually probe)
  M64 P3
  G4 P1.5

  #3059 = 1
  (PRINT, SET C REF: at A -45 one inch in front, puck UP. JOG the tip to where driving toward centre in +X would strike the puck, then press StartC -- it records the pose itself.)
  (DEBUG, SET C REF ready -- jog the tip, then press StartC)

o<cal_c_ref> endsub

M2 (end program)
